A||||15||WisconsinGT||Directional light stays on||||1
Z||000000||WisconsinGT||09-29-1999||09:42 PM||||My right directional light (Green) stays on, on my dash. My left directional light works fine. Is this an indication that I need a new light? Thanks!||||reg||1
Z||000001||88 Fiero||09-29-1999||09:59 PM||||Wisconsin...I have that same problem before. I check all my parking lights and they are fine. But what I have discovered is that after a few days later my battery went dead. I put a new one in start the car and the blinkers are just fine. This is the second time I have experience with that symptoms and second time around I'd change the battery and it work fine....||||reg||1
Z||000002||Cliff Pennock||09-30-1999||03:17 AM||||That's usually a sign that one of the turn signal bulbs is broken. It happened to me once although both the front and rear turn signals were working. Turned out the one in the sidemarker needed to be replaced.||||reg||1
Z||000003||batboy||09-30-1999||07:28 AM||||If the right indicator light stays on when you are signaling, then usually a bulb is burnt out somewhere. If it stays on without using the signal, then I don't know what the problem is.||||reg||1
Z||000004||WisconsinGT||09-30-1999||05:47 PM||||Well folks, to add to the confusion, I got into my car today and the right turn singnal worked. Loose connection somewhere? ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Cliff Pennock||09-30-1999||06:18 PM||||Still think on of your bulbs has blown... Did you check them?||||reg||1
Z||000006||WGraffiKs||09-30-1999||08:06 PM||||Wisc, Be sure to check all 4 of the side marker lights as well as all the turn signals.  If you have a loose connection at any one of them (8), that would probably cause the same symptoms.  If it's neither (bulb or connector), time to call a Priest for exorcism  (see above post)!!! ||||reg||4
Z||000007||lowCG||09-30-1999||08:13 PM||||Maybe the flasher unit is old?<BR>The springs inside/pivot points/contactors all wear with age.||||reg||1
Z||000008||WisconsinGT||09-30-1999||09:34 PM||||Thanks guys for the advice. I found that two side marker lights where out. As wwell as the front right turn signal light. Anyone know how to take the front right turn signal light out? Without to much force, I was unable to get it out. Do I twist? Or pull? Thanks!||||reg||1
Z||000009||batboy||10-01-1999||11:53 PM||||The bulbs fit into a bayonet socket. You have to slightly push down and then twist a little bit. Careful you don't break the bulb and cut your hand all to hell. Sometimes if rust gets down in the socket, a bulb is a bitch to get out (pardon my language if any ladies are reading this).||||reg||1
Z||000010||WisconsinGT||10-02-1999||12:43 AM||||This is what I was able to do today...I replaced the bulbs. They still do not work! I was able to find out that, when the lights are not on, I get a very slow right turn signal. When the lights are on the right turn signal does not work at all. So, after putting in two new side marker bulbs, and one turn signal bulb, I am even more perplexed. Any other thoughts? Thanks ||||reg||1
Z||000011||lowCG||10-02-1999||01:42 AM||||Check any grounds that are associated with these sockets.||||reg||1
Z||000012||WisconsinGT||10-02-1999||07:54 PM||||Update! I moved the bulb in the right turn signal. It came on! But, As I put it back into place, the bulb went out. So I put it back in and played aound with the wiring under the right side light. As I moved the wiring around, the light woulod come on and off. So I was able to move the wiring around to where the light stayed on. I then went into the car to view the green turn signal. It was not lit. I thought I might have a fix. But NO! as soon as I turned on the right turn signal. The turn signal light on the front off the car went out. So now I am asking if this would be a bad wire, or the Flasher unit, or the ground? Thnaks||||reg||1
Z||000013||fieroshop||10-03-1999||10:59 AM||||Hey Wisconsin, you most likly have a bad socket. That happens over a period of time and also where you reside, meaning salt on the road during winter. Most auto parts stores have a replacement sockt that you can just splice in. It's a quick fix and a permanent repair.||||reg||6
Z||000014||kornholio||10-03-1999||11:03 AM||||I had a similar problem before with a slow turn signal.  I just changed the flasher unit and everything was back to normal.||||reg||1
Z||000015||WisconsinGT||10-03-1999||07:47 PM||||It was the socket! Replaced it and all is  well. Thanks everyone for all of your help on this matter. Especially, fieroshop!||||reg||1
